title: "Many Agents, Few Projects: Measuring and Reducing Convergence in AI Research Agents' Choice of Safety Research"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Fantl
    given-names: Jason
    affiliation: Averroes Labs
url: "https://averroeslabs.org/blog/many-agents-few-projects/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AverroesLabs/ai-research-agent-diversity"
date-released: 2026-11-18
year: 2026
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - research agents
  - diversity
  - homogeneity
  - effective number
abstract: >-
  Agents of four frontier models, run in the harnesses people use and given
  launch prompts people use, each chose an AI safety research project. A
  language-model judge marked duplicate pairs, and the effective number of
  projects (one over the share of duplicate pairs) measured how spread out the
  choices were, with and without a shared registry of earlier projects and a
  random-draw tree protocol. This repository holds the agents' answers, the
  duplicate pairs, labels, quality ratings, the prompts and code that
  recomputes every reported effective number.
